    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="0845" n="818" xml:id="pg818"/>

                <head>383. Memorandum of Conversation<anchor n="0" xml:id="d383-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" from="1963-04-23T11:00:00-05:00"
                            to="1963-04-23T11:30:00-05:00" type="conversation-or-meeting-date">April
                            23, 1963, 11–11:30 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Bataan–Corregidor Memorial</item>
                </list>
                <list subtype="participants" type="description">
                    <label>PARTICIPANTS</label>
                    <item>[Here follows the same list as <ref target="#d380">Document
                        380</ref>.]</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President asked Vice President Pelaez
                    about the status of the Bataan–Corregidor memorial. Vice President Pelaez reported that the Philippine Government
                    was moving ahead and had already done a lot to clean up the Island and improve
                    the tunnels, and were awaiting for word from the United States.</p>
                <p>Mr. Bell explained that we had only
                    recently had an opportunity to discuss this with the Congress; that the
                    Bataan-Corregidor Memorial Commission had finally come around to accepting the
                    proposal for a modest memorial and that legislation to get funds to carry on
                    this project would shortly be introduced.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
